{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter S2b/S2c, runtime and factories agree, but users still see hand-maintained package help and the old two-family intercept behavior. Canonical generated artifacts may become authoritative only after the complete parser/route census is proven.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `scripts/gen_cli_help.py` with write and `--check` modes.\n\n- Enumerate canonical/compatibility/hidden routes from the immutable registry; resolve parser factories only in generation/check execution.\n- Render with S2a's fixed `prog`, width, formatter, ordering, UTF-8 LF, and trailing-newline policy.\n- Write one artifact per canonical help key; exact aliases reuse canonical bytes. Compatibility/hidden spellings render the same argument-definition helpers with approved alias `prog` and replacement epilog.\n- Generate the grouped overview from route group/order/visibility plus parser summaries. Canonical visible commands appear once; aliases are annotated rather than duplicated; hidden routes are omitted.\n- Fail `--check` on any missing/stale/stray artifact, unresolved factory, non-deterministic second render, registry/parser census mismatch, or generated package-data diff.\n- Keep curated explanations/examples inside parser descriptions/epilogs or later editorial reference sections; no hand-authored usage line or option table may be concatenated after generation.\n\nCut top-level overview/help/unknown routing to the registry and committed artifacts. The lexical pre-scan handles global config-prefix token shape, command identity, `rebar help <command>`, and a first `--help`/`-h` token after the spelling. It must complete before RP-04 snapshot, config parsing/materialization, mount, handler/factory resolution, or optional imports. Free-text `--help` later in argv remains data/handler input as today.\n\nApproved behavior changes: the 21 formerly intercept-only help forms now succeed safely; overview grouping changes; help output becomes deterministic parser-rendered text. Unknown/help streams and exit codes, historical `jira-onboard`, hidden `bridge-status`, and unknown `purge-bridge` remain as specified.\n\n## Out-of-directory consumers of the help surface (census + disposition)\nThe cutover changes package help data that consumers OUTSIDE `src/rebar/_cli/help/` read. Each is enumerated with its disposition; none is left implicit:\n\n- `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` + its `docs/cli-reference.md` CI drift gate — reads `rebar._cli._help.known_subcommands()` and renders `_help.subcommand_help(name)` verbatim, and drift-gates its `INTERCEPT_COMMANDS` key set against `rebar._cli.__init__.ladder_intercepts()`. Disposition: KEPT WORKING by contract. `_help.known_subcommands()`/`subcommand_help()`/`overview()` remain the public read API but now read GENERATED `help/*.txt` (written by `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`) instead of hand-captured text; the reader signatures are unchanged, so `gen_cli_reference.py` needs no code change. `docs/cli-reference.md` is REGENERATED through that script's `--check` gate as an APPROVED doc delta reflecting the new overview grouping and the 21 now-succeeding help forms. Both `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` and `docs/cli-reference.md` are in file_impact.\n\n- Tests that pin `known_subcommands()`/`overview()` shape or the intercept set — `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py` (routing vs `known_subcommands()` vs `overview()` agreement, `^  <sub>` overview line shape, `_OVERVIEW_ALLOWLIST`), `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_coverage.py` (consumes `known_subcommands()`), `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes_doc_conformance.py` and `test_exit_codes_doc_conformance_heldout.py` (`set(known_subcommands()) | _INTERCEPTS`), `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py`, and `tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py`. Disposition: UPDATED as APPROVED deltas — overview grouping/uniqueness and the retired intercept-only forms change these expectations; each is updated to assert the new registry/artifact-derived shape, and the pre-operation-boundary sentinels in `test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py` are extended to the new help pre-scan. All are in file_impact.\n\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py` — the docs-reference generator's own unit tests, which exercise `known_subcommands()`/`subcommand_help()`. Disposition: re-run and updated only where the generated-artifact re-sourcing changes an asserted value; in file_impact.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nThe existing execution ladder remains active. Commit generator, artifacts, route-help lookup, and subprocess tests together. Reverting this task restores the old help family without changing runtime grammar or stored data.\n\n## Testing\nUse generator unit tests and real CLI subprocess tests in a fresh attachable checkout. Sentinels raise if help/unknown paths compose an operation snapshot, read config, mount/create a store, resolve a parser/handler, or import heavy optional modules. Assert exact artifact bytes, streams, exit codes, overview uniqueness/grouping, every alias class, malformed global syntax, free-text negative control, and a normal execution control that still crosses operation/mount boundaries.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` proves every registered help artifact and overview are deterministic, parser-derived, complete, and free of stale/stray resources.\n- [ ] Every visible canonical command appears once in the grouped overview; exact aliases reuse bytes and compatibility/hidden/retired spellings follow the approved rules.\n- [ ] Both top-level help forms return exact committed generated bytes before operation/config/store/parser/handler/optional-import boundaries.\n- [ ] Free-text later `--help`, malformed global syntax, unknown commands, streams, and exit codes match the explicit compatibility contract.\n- [ ] A normal execution negative control still reaches RP-04 operation composition and established mount/init behavior through the old execution ladder.\n- [ ] No hand-maintained usage or option table remains in package help."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787270949764922001,"uuid":"2e9be748-f173-4f79-95e5-93ce2b5967e5"}